# AGENTIC-WORKFLOW-ROOT-GITIGNORE (two-repo delivery model — STEP 6.6)
# ============================================================================
# Project root .gitignore — developer's workflow repo (Option 1: two separate repos)
# ============================================================================
# This file is for the OPTIONAL developer git repo at the project root. That repo
# versions Agentbase and Docbase (workflow environment + docs/memory).
#
# Codebase is its OWN independent git repo and is delivered SEPARATELY to the customer.
# Therefore it is IGNORED here — the developer clones the top-level repo (Agentbase + Docbase)
# and clones or links Codebase **separately**; the customer clones only Codebase
# (clean). The two repos do not know each other.
#
# Detail: bootstrap.md → STEP 6.6 and INVARIANT RULES item 1.
# ============================================================================

# --- Codebase: separate repo + customer delivery (real directory or worktree symlink) ---
# ROOT-ANCHORED (leading /): only Codebase at the project root is targeted.
# Unanchored "Codebase" matches at EVERY level in git (e.g. Agentbase/docs/Codebase/...) — unwanted.
/Codebase
/Codebase/

# --- Codebase git worktree directories (tied to Codebase git; not tracked in the top-level dev repo) ---
/Codebase-wt-*/

# --- OS / editor noise ---
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- Optional: uncomment below to also exclude a sensitive memory vault from the dev repo (opt-in) ---
# Docbase/memory/

# END-AGENTIC-WORKFLOW-ROOT-GITIGNORE (end of managed block — repair/normalize rewrites the block up to this line)
